    "created_at": "2026-03-17T09:23:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-17T09:23:53Z",
    "body": "Hi @nchevobbe, thanks for the ping. From the Chromium perspective, I don't have any objections to the current direction of the PR.\r\n\r\nTo address your specific points:\r\n\r\n* Interface vs. Namespace: Moving to a ConsoleContext interface is a good call and aligns with how we’ve approached the implementation in Chromium. It feels more robust than a generic namespace object for this purpose.\r\n* Spec Organization: Keeping the method definitions under the existing console section seems like a pragmatic way to avoid duplication for now. As long as the WebIDL linkage is clear, I don't see it as a major issue.\r\n* State Interaction: I agree that the interaction with internal states like the group stack needs careful thought, but I don't think it should be a blocker for the initial specification of .context(). Since similar challenges already exist with multiple documents, we can iterate on this in a follow-up issue",
    "author_association": "NONE",
